 [17592186536983 1072 #uuid "00623118-ee32-53b0-8e64-30db43b56fa6" 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536983 1074 "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,dV={∭}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,z)\\,r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the formulas\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/d2/d2b3344b7b910f5685d4fd81b75a600608af6b008778ff608cb084edb5a92da9.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is one-half of a right vertical cylinder of radius $2$ whose axis passes through the point $(2,0)$ in the $xy$-plane, and is\n\n- bounded below by $z=0,$ and\n\n- bounded above by $z=1.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now write the $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ in polar coordinates:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =4 \\\\ (r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta-2)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2} & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta+4+{r}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta & =4 \\\\ {r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )-4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ {r}^{2}-4r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta & =0 \\\\ r(r-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $r$ cannot be identical to zero on the entire semicircle, we must have $r=4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}.$\n\nAs a result, in cylindrical polar coordinates, our region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta ,z)\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)},\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2},\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}x^{2} + y^{2}\\,\\text{d}V & ={∭}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta)^{2}+(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta)^{2})\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={∭}_{Δ}{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\cdot r\\,dz\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536984 1080 "{\\int }_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{- 2 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-4}^{r \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 1}\\frac{r}{\\sqrt{r^{2} + 2}}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536984 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536984 1083 #uuid "0525826c-a736-5227-9f0a-27dd1c50c845" 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536985 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{-2}^{r \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}r \\sqrt{r^{2} + 1}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536985 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536985 1083 #uuid "098d3517-e148-57fb-b802-0b2dbc349278" 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536986 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{4 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{1}^{2}r^{3}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536986 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536986 1083 #uuid "0a83957d-072f-56dd-967f-e6e3cad6b479" 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536987 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)}}{\\int }_{4}^{7}r^{2}\\,dz\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536987 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536987 1083 #uuid "0da30d8b-b4d8-596a-8c80-6b14e0374096" 13194139535887 17592186045443 true] [17592186536988 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{8 \\cos{\\left(\\